{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1508747-shared-fetters","id":1508747,"title":"Shared Fetters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-18T07:33:18-07:00","id":1508747,"title":"Shared Fetters?","content":"Can multiple Wraiths be connected to the same Fetter? For example, a family heirloom or a royal crown passed down across generations. Can this single Fetter be used to control those multiple Wraiths, like a familial line in the examples above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27764-hasnamuss","name":"Hasnamuss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27764_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T08:27:28-07:00","id":1508751,"title":"","content":"There's no reason an object or person can't be the fetter for more than one Wraith. The Titanic is likely the fetter for more than one wraith. <br /> <br /> Note that it isn't that the item is more metaphysically important in itself, just that multiple wraiths have a strong connection to it for their own reasons. In your family heirloom example each wraith will have his or her own personal attachment to the object and they may have very different emotional characters. The successor, the abdicator, and the usurper will all have a unique relationship to the crown, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7